# PatternFly 6 Migration Rules for Foreman

## Documentation

Always reference these files when generating or editing PatternFly code:
- `AGENT.md` — project migration guide, architecture, and coding standards
- `.claude/instructions/pf6-migration-patterns.md` — before/after code recipes for all migration types
- `.claude/instructions/pf6-testing-recipes.md` — PF6-specific test patterns
- `migration-toolkit/checklists/` — phase-by-phase migration checklists

## Import Rules

- NEVER import from `@patternfly/react-core/deprecated` — use composable equivalents
- NEVER import from `@patternfly/react-core/next` — use standard imports
- NEVER import from `@patternfly/react-table/deprecated` — use composable Table
- NEVER import from `patternfly-react` or `patternfly` (PF3 legacy)
- ALWAYS use `@patternfly/react-charts/victory` for chart components
- ALWAYS use `@patternfly/react-core` for all PF components
- Use `import { translate as __ } from '../../common/I18n'` for all user-visible strings

## CSS Rules

- Use `--pf-t--global--*` semantic design tokens for colors, spacing, fonts
- Use `--pf-v6-c-*` for component-level CSS variable overrides
- NEVER use `pf-v5-` prefixed CSS class names
- NEVER use `--pf-v5-*` CSS variables
- NEVER hardcode hex/rgb colors — use PF6 design tokens for dark mode compatibility
- Co-locate SCSS with components: `ComponentName/ComponentName.scss`

## Component Rules

- ALWAYS use functional React components with hooks
- Use `useSelector` and `useDispatch` for Redux state (NEVER `connect()` HOC)
- Use `useState`, `useEffect`, `useMemo`, `useCallback` for local state
- Props must be destructured in function signature
- Use PF6 composable patterns:
  - Modal: `<Modal>` + `<ModalHeader>` + `<ModalBody>` + `<ModalFooter>`
  - Dropdown: `<Dropdown>` + `<MenuToggle>` + `<DropdownList>` + `<DropdownItem>`
  - Select: `<Select>` + `<MenuToggle>` + `<SelectList>` + `<SelectOption>`
  - Table: `<Table>` + `<Thead>` + `<Tbody>` + `<Tr>` + `<Th>` + `<Td>`
  - EmptyState: headingText/icon as props, not child components

## Testing Rules

- Use React Testing Library (`render`, `screen`, `waitFor`) — NEVER Enzyme
- Query by role first: `screen.getByRole('button', { name: '...' })`
- Use `@testing-library/user-event` (not `fireEvent`) for interactions
- Wrap router-dependent components in `<MemoryRouter>`
- PF6 buttons wrap text in span — use `getByRole` not `getByText` for buttons
- PF6 dropdown menus only render when open — click toggle before querying items

## Foreman-Specific Rules

- One directory per component: `ComponentName/index.js` + `.scss` + `__tests__/`
- Index pages use `<IndexPage columns={[...]} />` shared component
- Detail pages registered in `resourceConfigs.js`
- SPA routes registered in `routes/IndexPages/index.js`
- Plugin extensibility via Fill/Slot pattern
